---
type: statement
kind: remark
slug: riccati-affine-formulation
---

By [%full (e)](statement:affine-process-definition-remark) and linearity of differentiation, the differential equation in [%full](statement:affine-regularity) is equivalent to the following system of equations.
$$
  @tag(complex-riccati-system)
  \forall ~ \stateVar \in \stateSpace, \qquad \left\{\begin{aligned}
    \dot\aff(t, \momentVar, \stateVar) &= \ode\big(\affPart(t,\momentVar), \stateVar\big) & t \geq 0 \\
    \aff(0,\momentVar, \stateVar) &= \prj{\momentVar}{\stateVar}
  \end{aligned}\right.
$$
